  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "If $U={1,2,3,...,100}$ is the universal set and $S={1,3,5,...,99}$, then $\\overset{\u2015}{S}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $S,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{S},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $S.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the integers $1$ through $100,$ while the set $S$ consists of the odd integers $1$ through $99.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $S$ are the even integers $2$ through $100.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $S$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{S}={2,4,6,...,100}.\n$$",
